{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Collection Item","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300404024","type":"Type"}],"id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/library/11799","identified_by":[{"classified_as":[{"_label":"repository number","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300404621"}],"content":"11799","type":"Identifier"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"call number","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300311706"}],"content":"PZ3 .P9476","type":"Identifier"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"preferred term","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300404670"}],"content":"The past recaptured  ","type":"Name"}],"produced_by":{"carried_out_by":[{"_label":"Proust, Marcel,","id":"actor/proust-marcel","type":"Actor"},{"_label":"A. \u0026 C. Boni","id":"actor/a-and-c-boni","type":"Actor"}],"timespan":{"_label":"1932","begin_of_the_begin":"1932-01-01T00:00:00Z","end_of_the_end":"1932-01-01T00:00:00Z","type":"TimeSpan"},"type":"Production"},"referred_to_by":[{"classified_as":[{"_label":"inscription statement","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435414"}],"content":"abq copy : fair condition.|SColl abq : Annotation by unknown on front loose endpaper : 369 ; annotation by unknown on p. 369.|SColl abq : Inscription on half t.p. from Edward Dahlberg to Alfred Stieglitz, January 26, 193[?] : My dear Alfred Stieglitz - Life at / its apex is such an allegory that / the rare men of this world are not / only deemed Fooes of Paradise by the bread / and bean realists but are reckoned never / to have existed at all. For this reason / the Existence of christ is denied, the / authorship of Hamlet doubted - So I write / not as famous, for any man with a thick / enough wit can go colliding against / the crust of this planet and get a prize / for it, but as an incredible myth - The / man does not exist, for how can such an / incredibly innocent, foolishly good / man live in such a foolproof wicked / world. But I believe in myths, in Fools, / in Lear, in [Tomin], in you. And so in the / same spirit, to defame fame + to forswear / all the vain realities of this all too / real world, I am and remain / your loving, non-existent friend, / Edward Dahlberg / N.Y.C., / Jan. 26, 3[?].","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"description statement","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416"}],"content":"Ephemera found in front of dedication p. : Newspaper clipping : Proust's First-Published Writings by Harry Levin, The New York Times, August 1, 1948.\nGeorgia O'Keeffe Personal Library.","type":"LinguisticObject"}],"representation":[],"type":"HumanMadeObject"}